{
  "id": "account-compromise-chain",
  "name": "Account Compromise Chain (Docker, Wazuh SIEM)",
  "description": "CSC3117 Week 9/10 Kill Chain / ATT&CK and incident-response triage lab. A Kali attacker brute-forces SSH into 'victim' (jdoe / password123), logs in, then creates a backdoor account or edits sudoers. victim ships logs to a Wazuh manager + indexer + dashboard so the whole chain (repeated auth failures, the success, the privilege-escalation step) shows up as SIEM alerts for the class to map to the Kill Chain and MITRE ATT&CK. See docs/labs/account-compromise-chain.md for the attack command, the dashboard walkthrough and the reset-for-a-re-run steps. All three Wazuh roles disable inter-node TLS for lab simplicity (isolated Docker network only) and, like several other bundled Docker roles, are not integration-tested against a live engine.",
